"The selected communications stack also reflects the framework already used by the project. Spring's message broker configuration maps application sends and subscriptions to explicit prefixes, while STOMP provides named destinations and message frames over the SockJS endpoint. A raw WebSocket protocol could carry events but would require the application to define more of its own routing conventions. Polling over REST would simplify infrastructure but introduce repeated requests and slower update discovery. The selected arrangement gives the project a clear event model, while the simple broker remains process-local and does not provide a distributed queue or cross-instance coordination."
