"Message persistence uses the Room document as the aggregate boundary. The handler resolves the room, constructs a Message with a timestamp and appends it to the room's list before publishing the message to subscribers. This ordering means that a message delivered through this handler has first passed the room lookup and save operation. The source does not implement a transaction spanning MongoDB and broker delivery, nor a durable outbox. If the database save succeeds and broker publication fails, a later history read may reveal a message that active subscribers did not immediately receive. Conversely, a client retry after an uncertain connection result could submit a duplicate because messages do not have a stable client or server idempotency key."
